# E134: Go linker mmap permission denied on HMDFS

error_signature: link: mapping output file failed: permission denied|go build.*link.*permission denied
root_cause: Go linker uses mmap syscall to efficiently write ELF output files. On HMDFS (HarmonyOS Distributed File System) or SELinux-restricted filesystems, mmap write operations may be denied even when normal file write permissions exist. TMPDIR workaround does not help because the issue is with mmap permissions, not /tmp access.
match_keywords: go build,link,mapping output file,permission denied,mmap,HMDFS,Go linker
rec_description: Go linker fails to create output binary due to mmap permission restrictions on HMDFS. This is a platform-specific limitation that cannot be fixed by environment variables alone.
rec_command: |Try alternative approaches:
  1. CGO_ENABLED=1 with -linkmode=external -extld=clang (uses external linker)
  2. Build in different filesystem (non-HMDFS directory)
  3. Check SELinux policies for mmap restrictions
  4. Use pre-compiled Go binaries from upstream releases
  5. Report as platform limitation if no workaround found
affected_scope: All Go projects compiled on HMDFS filesystems (croc, Go tools, etc.)
verification_cmd: go build -v -x -ldflags="-s -w" -o test_binary . 2>&1 | grep "mapping output file"
category: platform|filesystem|mmap|Go
severity: 4
priority: 3
trigger_tool: go|go build
stage: compilation

